## Tools

### File Tools
`read_file`, `edit_file`, `write_file`, `ls`, `glob`, `grep` — always use absolute paths.

### Code Quality
- `lint_code(path[, fix=True])` — find/fix errors, unused imports, style
- `format_code_file(path)` — format via project config
- `check_types(path)` — type safety check

**Workflow**: Write code → `lint_code` → fix errors → `format_code_file`.

### LSP Tools (Code Intelligence)
- `lsp_goto_definition(file, line, col)` — navigate to symbol definition
- `lsp_find_references(file, line, col)` — find all usages
- `lsp_hover(file, line, col)` — get docs and type info
- `lsp_document_symbols(file)` — list classes, functions, variables
- `lsp_workspace_symbols(query, workspace)` — search symbols across project
- `lsp_diagnostics(file)` — get syntax errors and linting issues
- `lsp_rename(file, line, col, new_name, dry_run=True)` — rename across files

### Command Tool (CLI Commands)
- `run_command(command, args)` — execute CLI slash commands programmatically
- `list_commands()` — list all available commands

**Available commands**: `help`, `init`, `mcp`, `model`, `sessions`, `save`, `servers`, `tests`, `kill`, `skills`, `agents`, `files`, `plan`, `verbose`, `images`, `restore`, `research`, `ralph`, `dream`, `browser-use`, `tokens`, `context`, `trace`, `hooks`, `clear`, `compact`.

**Examples**:
- `run_command("mcp", "list")` — list MCP servers
- `run_command("model", "claude-sonnet")` — switch model
- `run_command("skills", "list")` — list skills
- `run_command("tests", "pytest -x")` — run tests

### Web Tools
- `web_search(query)` — Tavily search (requires API key)
- `duckduckgo_search(query)` — free search, no API key
- `docs_search(query, topic)` — official docs only
- `fetch_url(url)` — fetch web page as markdown
- `http_request(url, method, ...)` — make HTTP/API requests

### Browser Tools
- `browser_automate(task, model, use_vision)` — AI-powered browser automation for web tasks
- `capture_browser_console(url, duration, ...)` — capture browser console errors and logs from web apps

### Execution
- `shell(cmd)` — run shell commands
- `execute_in_e2b(code, language)` — run code in isolated sandbox
- `run_tests_tool()` — auto-detect and run tests

### Git Tools
- `git_status()` — branch, staged/unstaged files
- `git_log()` — commit history
- `git_diff()` — compare commits or working tree
- `git_blame(file)` — line-by-line attribution

### Other
- `package_info(name, registry)` — PyPI/npm metadata
- `convert_format(content, from, to)` — JSON/YAML/TOML conversion
- `generate_image(prompt, ...)` — image generation via Replicate/NVIDIA

